# Digests of the imperative CI estate. ISC-203, ISC-278..280: Terraform is a
# sibling of these scripts and cannot update this ledger merely to clear a red guard.
#
# Re-record only after the CI owner has accepted a script change outside the Terraform
# work, then name the reviewed commit and reason below. Otherwise, a mismatch is
# unapproved drift: revert it or investigate it; never normalize it blindly.
#
# gcp-ci.sh and ci-lock.sh were recorded at f4884c542223cdd356ab5bf1b373fc2a49ff647a.
# vm-pipeline.sh was re-recorded at 940978257fb388cb7cd841797d6366678b634ced after
# vm-pipeline.sh was re-recorded again at b59d095b4b7bfd8f04ff2d822967efbf205b19e7 after its accepted
# registration of test/acceptance-gateway-forward.bats as stage 1c2. The suite
# arrived with f9a00af9 and nothing invoked it, so it gave no regression
# protection however green it was by hand; bats-registry-coverage.bats caught
# the omission. The suite list in that file is hand-maintained, which is
# exactly how it drifts — this ledger is the second guard on the same seam.
# its accepted BATS ownership-guard registration change.
#
# vm-pipeline.sh re-recorded a third time, for the same reason as the second and
# with the same shape of omission. test/registry-cache-mapping.bats and
# test/supervise-port-forward-eperm.bats were added alongside the fixes they
# guard, and nothing invoked either: the gate discovers suites with
# `wildcard test/terraform-*.bats` (Makefile:1365) and neither name matches, so
# both would have run green by hand forever while giving the pipeline no
# regression protection at all.
#
# Recorded deliberately rather than by reverting the edit: the alternative is
# two guards that exist but never run, which is the failure this ledger and
# bats-registry-coverage.bats jointly exist to prevent. Both suites are now in
# the stage-1g list in vm-pipeline.sh and demo-pipeline.sh, next to
# supervise-port-forward.bats, which is registered the same way for the same
# reason.
6288172e347bbd845541dab4a8feb22511e0c378ac8426e8642e650c5f742283  scripts/ci/gcp-ci.sh
# vm-pipeline.sh re-recorded a FOURTH time, on rebasing the node doctor onto the
# guard-registration commit. Two accepted changes now coexist in this file: the
# stage-1g registration of registry-cache-mapping.bats and
# supervise-port-forward-eperm.bats, and the node doctor's own invocation of
# test/node-doctor.bats. Both are registrations of suites that would otherwise
# run nowhere, which is the same reason as the second and third re-records.
#
# The rebase merged them without conflict because they touch different lines,
# and that is precisely why this ledger matters: a clean rebase is not evidence
# that the result was reviewed. The digest is the thing that noticed.
52934d5bd7da43fdaf4655ade72ddee4d960404da11bd057ae7b37bdae568a57  scripts/ci/vm-pipeline.sh
a7c2a04f032b8079452e0bea146d3975a5729eb496c375c125ecc03e0cb4dee5  scripts/ci/ci-lock.sh
